{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355207-unchained-in-manch-vegas-session-1-recap","id":1355207,"title":"Unchained in Manch-Vegas: Session 1 Recap","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-16T10:19:36-08:00","id":1355207,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Unchained in Manch-Vegas: Session 1 Recap","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">My players and I had our first session last night. One of the players couldn't make it, but we managed to a small prologue in after I fixed everyone's character sheets. The setting takes place in Manchester, NH. Locally known as Manch-Vegas, even though there aren't any actual casinos or any resemblance to Los Vegas.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cast:</span></span></b><ul><li><b>Liberty Griswald</b> - Guardian/Tempter. Works as a Bodyguard for the Empire Security Company.</li> <li><b>Alan Thorn</b> - Psychopomp/Inquisitive. Works as a Programmer for a startup tech company.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Campaign Report:</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alan Thorn (PC) was on a planned business trip with the CEO of his company Jaymes Linburg. As part of company policy they hired a bodyguard through Empire Security Service to escort them to the airport. Liberty Griswald </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(PC) </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">acted as their bodyguard and driver. When both demons began speaking in Ancient Latin and Greek they realized what each other was. Both signaled to the other non-aggression, but even for the Unchained, such assurances are not to be trusted.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On their way, they encountered a police roadblock. Liberty thought nothing of the incident, but Alan could sense that the detour was orchestrated by the God-Machine. He could see the gears turning beyond the barrier, but decided to see how this played out.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On the detour route, a tree was blocking the way forward and three armed individuals approached the car. They asked for Jaymes, who was meditating with noise cancelling headphones on, unaware of the situation. One of them leveling a gun at Liberty in the driver's seat.<br /> <br /> Liberty smashed the car door into the man and bent reality to dispatch all three men in quick succession with his pistol (Merciless Gunman). Investigating the attacker\u2019s bodies Liberty was able to figure out that they were all Sleeper Agents activated to kidnap Jaymes. Liberty stole money from their wallets and Alan transferred money from the attacker\u2019s bank account into his offshore account.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Liberty called in the police and took his clients to a nearby hospital. To keep their cover intact Alan faked an injury. At the hospital, Officer Daniel Woodward questioned the three individuals about what happened. Alan had a preexisting relationship with the officer, who was suspicious of Alan being a Russian spy, due to Alan beating up a mugger and swearing in Russian. He warned Liberty of associating with Alan. When Liberty asked about the police roadblock Officer Daniel told him that there were no police roadblocks on their route and that Officer McShane was not a real officer. Officer Woodward let Liberty know that there will be an investigation, but that he shouldn\u2019t worry because he was defending his client.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Liberty and Alan agree to meet up at the Crossroads Tavern, a Demon hangout, to investigate what the God-Machine was planning to do with Jaymes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">GM Notes:</span></span></b><ul><li><b>Preparation</b><ul><li>Initially my goal for this session was to:<ul><li>Establish the God-Machine as increasing efforts into New Hampshire.</li> <li>Establish the hints of a bigger plot.</li> <li>Establish a Free Agency or Demon safe haven for the players to be able to have a way to communicate with other Demons.</li> <li>Incorporate some of the player\u2019s backstories.</li> </ul></li> <li>Work I did before hand:<ul><li>Created Reference Guide for Demon Players and Storyteller.</li> <li>Wrote various quick reference NPC character sheets for Demons, Angels, Stigmatics, and Cryptids.</li> <li>Created a brief guide of the city of Manchester, NH.</li> <li>Organizing reference documents for myself</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b>Session Start</b><ul><li>Asked players if they wanted to establish themselves as Ring at session start or should we introduce everyone one at a time. They decided to go with not knowing each other.</li> <li>They established that Alan and his boss were on their way to a meeting in California.</li> <li>It took the players a while to figure out how to hint to each other that they were Demons. We decided to go with each of them speaking \u201cdead\u201d languages. (I know the rules state only existing native languages, but my head canon is that there are a couple of cults or immortals who are native speakers that exist in the world)</li> <li>Needed some conflict to happen so added in the roadblock. One of the players passed, but the other failed. The passing player decided to follow the trap and let it happen.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>What could I have done better:</b><ul><li>I didn\u2019t explain resolving Conditions very well.</li> <li>While the players like the setting, they are still getting used to the system.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>What went well:</b><ul><li>Established that the Demon Players don\u2019t know everything.</li> <li>Established how even the most mundane interaction could be orchestrated by the God-Machine.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>What do I need to not forget:</b><ul><li>That the God-Machine has failed to kill Jaymes Linburg.<ul><li>What consequences will this have?</li> <li>Does the God-Machine still need him dead?</li> </ul></li> <li>Alan Thorn<ul><li>Alan has stolen money from Sleeper Agent bank accounts. Put into off-shore account.</li> </ul></li> <li>Liberty Griswald<ul><li>Killed three Sleeper Agents.</li> </ul></li> <li>Sleeper Agents<ul><li>The college had 3 Sleeper Agents as students, but there are likely more at the school.</li> <li>Who cared about these students? What will the fallout be?</li> <li>How will the God-Machine\u2019s agents respond to 3 Sleeper Agents being killed?</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b>Notes for Next Session:</b><ul><li>(Hook) Figure out who created three Sleeper agents and why.</li> <li>Bringing in Molly (PC) as a Private Investigator ally who can help them with their investigation.</li> <li>Establish Crossroads Tavern as a bar in a bolthole, run by a Demon fixer.</li> <li>\u200bGod-Machine failed to kill Jaymes. It\u2019s occult matrix must still be complete.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Please let me know what you think. Advice is greatly appreciated as this is my first DtD campaign.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u200b</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","user":"DontEatRawHagis","date":".  Edit: Formatting. 12-16-2019, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:52:04-08:00","id":1355239,"title":"","content":"Excellent write-up! I think it's a nice template for campaign reports. I'd like to know:<ul><li>Did the PC's decide why they Fell? If so, can you give a quick indication why?</li> <li>Any great dramatic moments or good quotes?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T06:34:17-08:00","id":1355387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355207-unchained-in-manch-vegas-session-1-recap?p=1355239#post1355239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the PC's decide why they Fell? If so, can you give a quick indication why?</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li><b>Liberty Griswald</b> - He was a Guardian Angel assigned to protect a child. He eventually grew bored, the child was not important to anything. When he let his guard down the child was run over by a school bus. The Guardian wasn't meant to protect the child because the child was important. The child's father was a scientist and without his son he became depressed and he put less effort into his work. The father made a mistake, causing his lab to blow up and destroy several families.</li> <li><b>Alan Thorn</b> - He was a Psychopomp assigned to ensure that humanity's technological capabilities progressed as at a slow, but safe rate. Instead he wanted to improve human technology faster. The result was his fall and subsequent goal of becoming head of the tech company he works for.</li> <li><b>Molly</b> - She was a Destroyer Angel assigned to kill a child who would eventually become a genocidal maniac. Instead she spared his life, not realizing the destruction that she was going to unleash.</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355207-unchained-in-manch-vegas-session-1-recap?p=1355239#post1355239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Any great dramatic moments or good quotes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here are a couple:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alan: I start programming on my computer and swear in an ancient dialect of Latin.<br /> Liberty: Do I know if this is a normal thing?<br /> Storyteller: He's a 20 something year old speaking a dialect of Latin that has either not been around for centuries or is only spoken by high up members of the Catholic clergy. Does that sound normal to you? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Liberty: *After shooting 3 men with Merciless Gunman* I run to the car and whisper &quot;Everyone stay here while I check if there is more of them.<br /> Jaymes: *Waking up* Oh my god! Whats happening?!<br /> Liberty: You sleep through 3 gun shots, but me whispering wakes you? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lt Daniel: I think Alan Thorn is a Russian Troll Hacker.<br /> Liberty: Why?<br /> Lt Daniel: When I interviewed him about his attempted mugging he swore in Russian at me.<br /> Alan (OOC): I was going to say I would never do that, but no I totally would. </div> </div> </div><br /> Dramatic Moment wise the players were keeping up a lot of banter. But when they encountered the Sleeper Agents in the woods they really felt the tension. And they realized that a lot of what they might assume is normal daily occurences might just be the God-Machine trying to screw with them.<br /> <br /> I'm glad I didn't have the God-Machine come after them directly and instead had the CEO to target. Didn't want to break their cover so soon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}